## Estate shell history: never lose bash history again
# One private repo (slade208/shell-history) holds every enrolled host's bash
# history: per-host capture with timestamps, a generated HISTORY.md with
# ==host== sections, and a hot-set window so Ctrl-R on any host finds
# commands run on any other. Every command hits disk immediately - crashed
# sessions lose nothing. Desktop is the regen owner.

## Am I enrolled?
echo $HISTFILE
# enrolled     -> ~/.shell-history/hosts/<hostname>.log
# not enrolled -> ~/.bash_history (the default)
# NOTE: $HISTFILE only updates in NEW shells - for the machine's true state:
grep -c 'shell-history' ~/.bashrc   # 0 = not enrolled, >0 = enrolled

## Enrol this host (any Linux box; idempotent)
# Requirements on the host: git, curl, ssh-keygen. NO GitHub tooling needed -
# the gh CLI is optional and only makes enrolment one-step.
bash -c "$(curl -fsSL operations.dev/hist-join.sh)"
# If gh is installed + logged in: fully automatic, done in one run.
# Otherwise the first run prints this host's deploy key; register it and re-run:
#   A) browser (any device): github.com/slade208/shell-history/settings/keys/new
#      title: <hostname> - tick 'Allow write access'
#   B) no browser on this box: gh auth login   (device flow - approve the
#      printed code from your phone), then re-run - the script adds the key
#      itself. It will also OFFER to install gh (dnf/yum/apt) if missing.
# Least privilege: the deploy key is all that's needed long-term - you can
# 'gh auth logout' after enrolment so no broad token stays on the host.

## Daily use
# ~/.shell-history/tooling/histgrep <pattern> [host]   search the whole estate
# Ctrl-R                                               includes other hosts' recent commands
# cat ~/.shell-history/HISTORY.md                      the whole estate, sectioned

## Restore
# Damaged local file:  git -C ~/.shell-history restore hosts/$(hostname -s).log
# Reimaged host:       re-run the enrol command - first shell has full history
# Point in time:       git -C ~/.shell-history log -p hosts/<host>.log

## Leave
# ~/.shell-history/tooling/leave.sh          remove hooks, keep clone
# ~/.shell-history/tooling/leave.sh --purge  also delete clone + key
